<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- G11a-2 fixture, written by hand for the parity harness of PPP (no source music): a D.S. al Coda over a repeat with endings. Bar 2 holds the segno and the forward repeat, bars 4 and 5 are the first and the second ending, "To Coda" ends bar 5, "D.S. al Coda" ends bar 6, the coda is bar 7. Bar 3 has a slashed grace on beat 1. Bar 6 ends on a D5 tied into the coda (bar 7): a tie that the written order leads into, and that the way back (5 then 7) does not. Played as written (the old player): 1 2 3 4 | 2 3 5 6 7 8 9. As an engraver reads it: 1 2 3 4 | 2 3 5 6 | 2 3 5 (To Coda) 7 8 9 (the repeat is not taken on the way back and the second ending is played). -->
